<title>UK: BOE revises shortage forecast to 1.7 bln stg.</title>
<headline>BOE revises shortage forecast to 1.7 bln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England revised its forecast of the money market shortage to 1.7 billion stg from the initial 1.85 billion stg.</p>
<p>The residual shortage at noon was 1.116 billion.</p>
<p>It invited a round of fixed rate operations, comprising 6.0 percent repos to March 21 and 24 and outright offers of bills maturing on or before March 24.</p>
</text>
